WEB SOURCE (the specification)
  web/src/features/settings/components/PrivacySection.tsx — a settings feature component (named export +
  default) rendered inside the Settings page. It composes FOUR client/remote seams and surfaces toasts:
    • useVersionInfo() → require_cookie_consent  (the lone remote read; /system/version)
    • lib/recentPages  → getRecentPages / clearRecentPages / subscribeRecentPages  (client LRU count)
    • lib/cookieConsent→ getConsent / setConsent / clearConsent / subscribeConsent  (tri-state)
    • lib/confirmSilence (via <ConfirmDialog silenceKey="clear-recent-pages">) — isSilenced / silence
    • useToast().success  (post-action feedback)   · useTranslation (t)
  Structure: GlassPanel.p-5 { header (IconBox cyan ShieldCheck + title + subtitle) ; recent-pages panel
  (title + body + "%count entries stored" + secondary "Clear recent pages" button disabled at count 0) ;
  consent panel (title + bodyOn/bodyOff by require_cookie_consent + tri-state label + primary "Re-grant
  consent" / secondary "Withdraw consent" / ghost "Reset", each disabled when its state is already active) }
  + a warning <ConfirmDialog> (silence checkbox; when previously silenced it fires onConfirm without
  rendering). Every conditional branch (consent on/off, the 3 consent-state labels, the 4 disabled
  predicates, the silence short-circuit) and every t() key was read end-to-end and reproduced 1:1.
  Charts/maps: none. States in source: the section is ALWAYS rendered (no data-gated hide).

